1
00:00:05,862 --> 00:00:07,409
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,411 --> 00:00:08,915
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors. Some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:22,192 --> 00:00:23,452
Planning to run again?

4
00:00:27,892 --> 00:00:29,525
If you're going to run, do it properly,

5
00:00:30,586 --> 00:00:32,212
so we never have to meet like this.

6
00:00:41,879 --> 00:00:43,259
Mom!

7
00:00:44,172 --> 00:00:45,365
My boy!

8
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:54,579
Mom, that must have been so hard.

9
00:00:55,199 --> 00:00:56,219
It was.

10
00:00:56,332 --> 00:00:59,672
Gyeol kept saying he wanted to see you,
so I brought him along.

11
00:00:59,779 --> 00:01:01,253
Did everything go all right?

12
00:01:03,405 --> 00:01:04,959
Here, eat this.

13
00:01:06,279 --> 00:01:08,011
You shouldn't have.

14
00:01:08,665 --> 00:01:10,071
You need to eat.

15
00:01:14,252 --> 00:01:16,047
I've seen him somewhere.

16
00:01:16,997 --> 00:01:18,145
Who was it?

17
00:01:18,774 --> 00:01:20,064
Where was it?

18
00:01:20,325 --> 00:01:22,281
I definitely know that face.

19
00:01:25,231 --> 00:01:27,344
Let's go, honey.

20
00:01:27,369 --> 00:01:28,498
Honey?

21
00:01:28,789 --> 00:01:31,103
Honey?

22
00:01:33,085 --> 00:01:35,530
Shall we? Gyeol, let's go.

23
00:01:35,555 --> 00:01:37,083
Honey, come on.

24
00:01:59,013 --> 00:02:00,866
That was her, wasn't it? Gyu Rim.

25
00:02:00,891 --> 00:02:02,278
I didn't mistake her, did I?

26
00:02:04,278 --> 00:02:06,560
All those years searching
and not a single trace of her,

27
00:02:06,674 --> 00:02:07,998
and here she is.

28
00:02:09,239 --> 00:02:10,499
What was she doing at a police station?

29
00:02:12,138 --> 00:02:13,661
That's not the point.

30
00:02:13,686 --> 00:02:17,355
She called that man
who looks like a monkey "honey."

31
00:02:17,398 --> 00:02:19,165
So that man is her husband?

32
00:02:22,791 --> 00:02:24,311
She's gone and married too?

33
00:02:25,766 --> 00:02:27,072
Her eyes must be broken!

34
00:02:27,185 --> 00:02:30,005
How could she leave you
for someone like that?

35
00:02:30,372 --> 00:02:32,178
And that kid? Her son?

36
00:02:33,559 --> 00:02:35,492
That doesn't add up.

37
00:02:35,517 --> 00:02:37,186
Not a chance.

38
00:02:38,148 --> 00:02:39,225
Jeong Woo.

39
00:02:39,965 --> 00:02:40,979
What?

40
00:02:42,492 --> 00:02:44,005
Drive for me.

41
00:03:01,366 --> 00:03:02,972
Sorry. Did I startle you?

42
00:03:03,351 --> 00:03:07,304
No need to apologize,
but what brought that on?

43
00:03:08,401 --> 00:03:10,088
Well, that was...

44
00:03:10,113 --> 00:03:13,179
I think she called you that
so that man wouldn't look down on her.

45
00:03:13,339 --> 00:03:14,339
Is that?

46
00:03:15,119 --> 00:03:17,098
If you're her husband,

47
00:03:17,123 --> 00:03:20,204
he can't push her around
and she has someone to rely on.

48
00:03:21,338 --> 00:03:22,407
Someone to rely on?

49
00:03:23,949 --> 00:03:24,986
Is it?

50
00:03:25,332 --> 00:03:28,147
But that doesn't mean I think
you're right for my mom,

51
00:03:28,172 --> 00:03:29,889
so don't get too excited.

52
00:03:33,992 --> 00:03:36,421
- Gyeol, no games starting today.
- What?

53
00:03:38,166 --> 00:03:39,635
And you,

54
00:03:39,809 --> 00:03:42,719
no matter how much he begs or threatens,
don't bring him to a place like this.

55
00:03:42,772 --> 00:03:44,125
It's not exactly somewhere worth going.

56
00:03:45,104 --> 00:03:47,966
Better to make sure
you never have to come here at all.

57
00:03:48,939 --> 00:03:51,252
So eat this tofu properly,

58
00:03:51,311 --> 00:03:54,484
and never end up somewhere
like this again. Understood?

59
00:03:55,286 --> 00:03:57,012
No games, really?

60
00:03:57,832 --> 00:04:00,392
Yes. I should've banned them ages ago.

61
00:04:00,532 --> 00:04:04,158
You said I could play
if I studied that hard.

62
00:04:04,225 --> 00:04:06,538
- Either way, no games.
- Where do I know that guy from?

63
00:04:06,563 --> 00:04:07,576
That's not fair.

64
00:04:07,601 --> 00:04:09,045
I know that face for sure.

65
00:04:09,047 --> 00:04:10,166
No games, and that's final.

66
00:04:10,330 --> 00:04:12,659
- Mom.
- I can't place him.

67
00:04:12,684 --> 00:04:13,834
Gyeol, enough.

68
00:04:13,859 --> 00:04:15,165
Wait for me!

69
00:04:25,450 --> 00:04:27,872
- Pull over.
- What?

70
00:04:28,399 --> 00:04:29,986
I said pull over.

71
00:04:40,685 --> 00:04:41,919
Hey!

72
00:04:51,439 --> 00:04:53,225
Why did you only ask
for a hundred thousand?

73
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,604
If you were taking money,
why not ask for a hundred million?

74
00:04:58,485 --> 00:05:00,378
Was I only worth
a hundred thousand dollars to you?

75
00:05:00,465 --> 00:05:01,858
What are you talking about?

76
00:05:04,532 --> 00:05:05,852
You said you wouldn't run.

77
00:05:07,472 --> 00:05:10,266
You promised you'd never run,
no matter what.

78
00:05:12,832 --> 00:05:14,074
I'm sorry.

79
00:05:14,945 --> 00:05:18,349
Sorry? You're sorry?

80
00:05:20,106 --> 00:05:22,665
Do you know how I lived
after you disappeared?

81
00:05:24,643 --> 00:05:27,943
For years I searched every corner
of the earth for you,

82
00:05:27,968 --> 00:05:32,359
out of my mind, living like a madman!

83
00:05:34,066 --> 00:05:38,572
And you got married, had a child,

84
00:05:39,192 --> 00:05:41,796
and you've been living just fine?

85
00:05:43,999 --> 00:05:45,962
- Mu Jin...
- Don't.

86
00:05:46,895 --> 00:05:48,878
How do you toy with someone like that?

87
00:05:49,892 --> 00:05:52,365
Who are you to toy with someone?

88
00:05:55,484 --> 00:05:57,418
Did you ever love me at all?

89
00:06:00,139 --> 00:06:03,219
Are you even human, you heartless woman?

90
00:06:27,112 --> 00:06:28,172
Come on, man.

91
00:06:31,605 --> 00:06:33,779
You've completely lost it.

92
00:06:37,546 --> 00:06:38,586
Kim Mu Jin!

93
00:06:47,552 --> 00:06:49,445
I'll walk for a bit.

94
00:06:49,958 --> 00:06:52,458
You're not thinking
anything stupid, are you?

95
00:06:52,598 --> 00:06:55,945
I keep telling you,
there are plenty of women out there.

96
00:06:56,845 --> 00:06:59,172
I'll be back before we open for dinner.

97
00:07:23,113 --> 00:07:27,794
(Suragan Side Dishes)

98
00:07:27,819 --> 00:07:31,111
That's right! It's him. That guy.

99
00:07:33,586 --> 00:07:35,182
It's him, right?

100
00:07:36,285 --> 00:07:37,856
You, at that restaurant nine years ago.

101
00:07:37,888 --> 00:07:39,765
The guy who kept saying he liked you...

102
00:07:42,399 --> 00:07:44,385
Right.

103
00:07:44,632 --> 00:07:46,712
But now that I think about it,
no, it wasn't.

104
00:07:46,879 --> 00:07:50,188
That guy and this guy look nothing alike.

105
00:07:50,269 --> 00:07:52,485
I must've gotten them mixed up.

106
00:07:52,516 --> 00:07:54,627
- Heung Sik.
- Yes?

107
00:07:54,741 --> 00:07:56,359
Why the terrible acting?

108
00:07:57,719 --> 00:08:01,583
Terrible acting? Me? Not at all.

109
00:08:04,472 --> 00:08:07,126
He does look similar,
but it isn't him, right?

110
00:08:07,151 --> 00:08:08,217
Right.

111
00:08:08,725 --> 00:08:11,256
I was confused for a second too,
so he must've been mistaken.

112
00:08:15,545 --> 00:08:17,978
Why? Was my acting terrible too?

113
00:08:18,226 --> 00:08:19,252
A little?

114
00:08:19,510 --> 00:08:21,673
Trust me. It wasn't him.

115
00:08:23,992 --> 00:08:26,752
Now that's a sight.

116
00:08:26,777 --> 00:08:28,810
You look just like a family.

117
00:08:29,265 --> 00:08:30,481
Let's go.

118
00:08:33,144 --> 00:08:37,881
Wouldn't it be lovely if you three
lived together like a real family?

119
00:08:37,906 --> 00:08:39,971
It's a lovely sight. Hold still.

120
00:08:41,004 --> 00:08:42,886
Stand closer together.

121
00:08:42,912 --> 00:08:44,285
That looks good.

122
00:08:44,292 --> 00:08:46,446
How can you just stand there
and let her talk?

123
00:08:47,118 --> 00:08:50,672
I've let this go long enough,
but this is too much.

124
00:08:50,925 --> 00:08:53,265
Who do you think you're pairing off?

125
00:08:53,465 --> 00:08:56,396
How would Han Gyu Rim
ever be family with you?

126
00:08:56,421 --> 00:08:57,452
Gyu Yeong.

127
00:08:58,606 --> 00:09:01,239
What's that fox doing here again?

128
00:09:01,264 --> 00:09:02,421
Right?

129
00:09:02,446 --> 00:09:04,265
It's a wish. Just a wish.

130
00:09:04,479 --> 00:09:06,285
Can't I even say what I hope for?

131
00:09:06,310 --> 00:09:07,590
Mom, that's enough.

132
00:09:07,678 --> 00:09:10,668
So why does your wish
have to be Han Gyu Rim?

133
00:09:10,693 --> 00:09:12,012
Go look somewhere else.

134
00:09:12,106 --> 00:09:14,866
For a woman on your son's level.

135
00:09:16,285 --> 00:09:18,672
Where are your manners
with an elder, seriously?

136
00:09:18,698 --> 00:09:20,750
Why hit me? Am I wrong?

137
00:09:20,775 --> 00:09:22,034
Everything I said was true.

138
00:09:22,226 --> 00:09:23,946
Gyeol, you tell her.

139
00:09:24,565 --> 00:09:26,172
Everything she said was true.

140
00:09:26,565 --> 00:09:29,598
True enough to earn a good smack.

141
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:31,592
Gyeol, you little...

142
00:09:31,617 --> 00:09:35,882
My Gyeol should be a judge
someday. Well said.

143
00:09:36,067 --> 00:09:37,260
What's with you?

144
00:09:37,262 --> 00:09:40,063
You used to say your mom was too good
even for Kim Woo Bin,

145
00:09:40,111 --> 00:09:42,839
and now she's fallen for that,
that freeloader of a man?

146
00:09:42,926 --> 00:09:47,805
What? Did you just call my son
a freeloader?

147
00:09:48,359 --> 00:09:52,186
You hundred-year-old fox tail.

148
00:09:52,259 --> 00:09:54,032
Mom, what are you doing? Let it go.

149
00:09:54,057 --> 00:09:56,924
Did you just call me a fox tail?

150
00:09:57,046 --> 00:09:58,852
Have you ever seen me play the fox?

151
00:09:58,892 --> 00:10:00,172
And have you seen otherwise?

152
00:10:00,272 --> 00:10:02,748
Have you ever seen my son
steal a grain of rice?

153
00:10:02,773 --> 00:10:04,474
- Back then...
- Come here.

154
00:10:04,565 --> 00:10:07,167
Gyeol, you'd better watch yourself too.

155
00:10:07,192 --> 00:10:09,870
It takes one moment to go
from a Han to a Cho, you little brat.

156
00:10:09,895 --> 00:10:11,697
Zip it. Can you not zip it?

157
00:10:12,218 --> 00:10:13,537
Why are you blaming me?

158
00:10:13,821 --> 00:10:16,754
You'll be a Cho now. Cho Gyeol.

159
00:10:19,039 --> 00:10:22,059
Who would ever take in a brat like her?

160
00:10:22,491 --> 00:10:24,172
If you ever bring home a girl like that,

161
00:10:24,234 --> 00:10:27,574
I'll dig myself a hole
and climb right in. Your call.

162
00:10:27,599 --> 00:10:29,639
Am I insane? Dating someone like her.

163
00:10:29,868 --> 00:10:32,101
I need to throw salt. Get me the salt.

164
00:10:32,126 --> 00:10:33,839
Even salt is wasted on her.
Enough, stop it.

165
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,781
Let go. I said it hurts.

166
00:10:35,806 --> 00:10:37,386
It hurts.

167
00:10:39,465 --> 00:10:41,527
That hurts.

168
00:10:43,607 --> 00:10:45,374
That really hurts.

169
00:10:45,746 --> 00:10:47,372
All brute strength and no sense.

170
00:10:48,306 --> 00:10:49,839
I'm going to bruise.

171
00:10:50,806 --> 00:10:53,845
- What is wrong with you?
- What?

172
00:10:53,939 --> 00:10:56,052
You barely ever come to the shop.

173
00:10:56,206 --> 00:10:58,103
Even if you'd heard what she said,
you'd have pretended not to,

174
00:10:58,124 --> 00:11:00,346
acted like you knew nothing,
and walked right out.

175
00:11:00,466 --> 00:11:04,765
So why come in today, picking fights
and tearing into everyone?

176
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:07,886
Because I refuse to be family
with that freeloader.

177
00:11:07,911 --> 00:11:10,304
What's wrong with Heung Sik?

178
00:11:11,336 --> 00:11:13,399
I've told you until I'm blue in the face.

179
00:11:13,439 --> 00:11:16,926
If you're going to see someone,
see someone half a step above you.

180
00:11:16,966 --> 00:11:19,346
You seem to be under some illusion.

181
00:11:19,486 --> 00:11:21,492
I'm not that impressive.

182
00:11:21,652 --> 00:11:24,718
I'm the one who's pathetic
and lacking and second-rate.

183
00:11:24,925 --> 00:11:28,629
Heung Sik is a thousand times,
a million times better than me.

184
00:11:28,654 --> 00:11:29,682
And?

185
00:11:29,972 --> 00:11:32,417
You're saying you'd marry that freeloader?

186
00:11:32,442 --> 00:11:34,377
I'd be grateful if he'd have me.

187
00:11:34,537 --> 00:11:36,039
Have you lost your mind?

188
00:11:36,064 --> 00:11:37,937
I've never been more clear-headed.

189
00:11:41,612 --> 00:11:43,156
Is this because that freeloader...

190
00:11:43,224 --> 00:11:46,959
once picked you up off the street
and it moved you?

191
00:11:47,198 --> 00:11:49,967
You saved his mother
when she collapsed too, didn't you?

192
00:11:50,099 --> 00:11:52,019
So doesn't that make you even?

193
00:11:52,052 --> 00:11:55,940
Without those two,
I'd have been dead years ago.

194
00:11:56,974 --> 00:11:57,978
And?

195
00:11:59,106 --> 00:12:02,361
Are you actually planning
to go somewhere with them?

196
00:12:03,012 --> 00:12:04,459
I'm completely against it.

197
00:12:04,497 --> 00:12:07,852
Nobody's asking you to marry him,
so why interfere in my life?

198
00:12:08,065 --> 00:12:11,105
Since when did you care about me so much?

199
00:12:11,458 --> 00:12:15,692
I'm worried you'll all ruin my life too.

200
00:12:16,012 --> 00:12:17,658
I'm begging you,

201
00:12:17,683 --> 00:12:21,307
when I introduce you as my family,
even if I can't be proud of you,

202
00:12:21,363 --> 00:12:24,304
at least don't leave me humiliated.

203
00:12:27,125 --> 00:12:29,466
Go back to the man you met
eight years ago.

204
00:12:29,519 --> 00:12:31,192
At least he had the looks.

205
00:12:31,426 --> 00:12:33,586
Why bring him up out of nowhere?

206
00:12:33,673 --> 00:12:34,952
You startled me.

207
00:12:35,118 --> 00:12:36,951
You were crazy about that man.

208
00:12:37,099 --> 00:12:39,238
You couldn't forget him.
You even talked in your sleep.

209
00:12:39,279 --> 00:12:40,399
When did I ever?

210
00:12:40,424 --> 00:12:42,287
Why are you suddenly shouting?

211
00:12:45,945 --> 00:12:49,199
See? So the feelings are still there.

212
00:12:49,224 --> 00:12:51,531
You never got over him.

213
00:12:54,006 --> 00:12:56,826
Stop talking nonsense,

214
00:12:56,892 --> 00:12:59,845
and if you're going to keep
clashing with her, don't come by again.

215
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:06,402
I try to give you advice...

216
00:13:08,871 --> 00:13:10,458
That's going to bruise.

217
00:13:28,503 --> 00:13:30,358
(No married couples allowed)

218
00:13:34,879 --> 00:13:37,227
Are you determined
to shut this place down?

219
00:13:44,118 --> 00:13:45,824
No couples, no married couples.

220
00:13:45,999 --> 00:13:47,705
How are you supposed to run a business?

221
00:13:47,752 --> 00:13:49,253
Whoever wants to come will come.

222
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:52,679
Is going under your life's dream?

223
00:13:55,072 --> 00:13:56,125
Something wrong?

224
00:13:57,232 --> 00:14:00,259
No. Aren't you busy?

225
00:14:01,194 --> 00:14:02,419
What is it?

226
00:14:03,331 --> 00:14:04,938
Do I need a reason to stop by?

227
00:14:05,252 --> 00:14:06,805
You said we should eat together.

228
00:14:09,139 --> 00:14:12,452
Sorry, let's do it another time.

229
00:14:13,431 --> 00:14:15,140
So something is wrong.

230
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:16,945
What is it?

231
00:14:18,231 --> 00:14:19,742
Just go.

232
00:14:21,251 --> 00:14:23,111
- Why?
- No reason.

233
00:14:25,453 --> 00:14:26,954
Go home. Not today.

234
00:14:27,248 --> 00:14:28,279
Give it to me.

235
00:14:28,304 --> 00:14:30,924
Go home and rest
before you cause more trouble.

236
00:14:32,475 --> 00:14:36,458
If this place goes under,
I might actually kill you.

237
00:14:51,697 --> 00:14:53,317
What is it?

238
00:14:55,772 --> 00:14:59,138
Mu Jin saw Gyu Rim today.

239
00:14:59,486 --> 00:15:00,932
Who's Gyu Rim?

240
00:15:01,518 --> 00:15:04,065
That Han Gyu Rim from back then?

241
00:15:09,799 --> 00:15:12,152
When? How? Doing what?

242
00:15:12,372 --> 00:15:15,804
Purely by chance,
like something out of a story.

243
00:15:18,784 --> 00:15:20,658
Should we really let him go like that?

244
00:15:20,771 --> 00:15:25,152
Seo Hyeon, what if he crashes the car
on the way home?

245
00:15:25,672 --> 00:15:28,289
Is she still pretty?
Does he still like her?

246
00:15:28,314 --> 00:15:29,930
Is he mad about her?

247
00:15:30,078 --> 00:15:31,635
Does he want to start over?

248
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:34,586
I shouldn't have told you.

249
00:15:39,205 --> 00:15:41,792
But you don't have to worry.

250
00:15:41,919 --> 00:15:43,894
How can I not worry?

251
00:15:43,919 --> 00:15:47,525
I watched Mu Jin fall apart
over Han Gyu Rim.

252
00:15:47,759 --> 00:15:50,538
I know exactly how much
he still likes her.

253
00:15:52,438 --> 00:15:53,883
Gyu Rim is married.

254
00:15:56,251 --> 00:15:57,517
She even has a son.

255
00:15:59,479 --> 00:16:00,946
She has a son?

256
00:16:00,971 --> 00:16:02,994
He didn't know it was her son,

257
00:16:03,019 --> 00:16:06,574
and there was trouble
over a game they were playing...

258
00:16:07,544 --> 00:16:10,264
That boy is how they ended up meeting.

259
00:16:10,492 --> 00:16:12,032
Her son is that old?

260
00:16:12,199 --> 00:16:13,704
How old is he?

261
00:16:14,479 --> 00:16:17,280
Eight years old, apparently.

262
00:16:17,765 --> 00:16:21,785
But Han Gyu Rim broke up with Mu Jin
eight years ago.

263
00:16:23,209 --> 00:16:24,893
Was she seeing two men at once?

264
00:16:51,545 --> 00:16:53,071
Is this place no good either?

265
00:16:57,785 --> 00:16:59,349
Did they change chefs here?

266
00:16:59,374 --> 00:17:00,494
Why does it taste like this?

267
00:17:04,259 --> 00:17:07,146
It's good. It tastes the same to me.

268
00:17:07,205 --> 00:17:08,758
If it's so good, eat it all yourself.

269
00:17:08,791 --> 00:17:10,697
Take it away. I can't stand the smell.

270
00:17:12,471 --> 00:17:14,685
Nothing I bring is ever good enough.

271
00:17:14,932 --> 00:17:17,291
Why has your appetite vanished like this?

272
00:17:17,985 --> 00:17:19,827
Maybe I'm dying. Who knows.

273
00:17:22,318 --> 00:17:23,921
Is this because you heard
Chairman Kim has a grandchild,

274
00:17:23,946 --> 00:17:26,052
and it's put you out of sorts?

275
00:17:27,105 --> 00:17:28,944
Their son is younger than Mu Jin,

276
00:17:28,951 --> 00:17:30,619
yet he's married with a child already.

277
00:17:30,625 --> 00:17:32,058
Who is Mu Jin?

278
00:17:32,739 --> 00:17:34,965
Why bring up a name I don't recognize?

279
00:17:38,371 --> 00:17:41,010
(Mu Jin)

280
00:17:49,543 --> 00:17:50,946
Yes. I'll call you back.

281
00:17:50,971 --> 00:17:52,736
You really didn't do anything?

282
00:17:53,052 --> 00:17:54,158
Do what, out of nowhere?

283
00:17:54,277 --> 00:17:57,710
Did you and Mother really do nothing
to Gyu Rim?

284
00:17:58,347 --> 00:17:59,852
What are you going on about?

285
00:17:59,854 --> 00:18:02,022
She isn't that kind of person.

286
00:18:02,065 --> 00:18:04,932
Even if the world were ending,
she wouldn't do that.

287
00:18:05,359 --> 00:18:08,158
You or Mother must have done something.

288
00:18:08,183 --> 00:18:10,176
What did you do?

289
00:18:10,792 --> 00:18:13,345
What on earth did you do to Gyu Rim?

290
00:18:13,579 --> 00:18:16,734
I don't know why you're calling
out of nowhere like this,

291
00:18:16,962 --> 00:18:19,039
but I told you clearly
eight years ago too.

292
00:18:19,064 --> 00:18:20,685
Mother and I did nothing.

293
00:18:20,710 --> 00:18:23,185
Han Gyu Rim came to us herself.

294
00:18:23,712 --> 00:18:26,531
She said she'd walk away from you
for a hundred thousand dollars.

295
00:18:26,859 --> 00:18:28,559
You heard it with your own ears.

296
00:18:33,199 --> 00:18:34,906
Are you still on about Han Gyu Rim?

297
00:18:35,618 --> 00:18:38,615
It's been years since it ended.
How long are you going to do this?

298
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:55,487
(Chairwoman Hong Ok Seon)

299
00:18:59,639 --> 00:19:00,652
It's about Mu Jin.

300
00:19:02,079 --> 00:19:03,106
I didn't ask.

301
00:19:04,499 --> 00:19:07,012
Couldn't you reach out to him first?

302
00:19:08,152 --> 00:19:10,310
He broke up with Han Gyu Rim
long ago anyway.

303
00:19:13,251 --> 00:19:15,811
She was a decent girl.

304
00:19:16,312 --> 00:19:17,891
You and I went too far.

305
00:19:18,239 --> 00:19:20,863
Why so much talk when I'm working?

306
00:19:21,224 --> 00:19:22,398
This is a company.

307
00:19:22,824 --> 00:19:24,536
Can't you separate work from personal?

308
00:19:29,846 --> 00:19:31,812
Is it that bad?

309
00:19:33,705 --> 00:19:34,706
The doctor...

310
00:19:36,928 --> 00:19:39,012
The doctor told me to prepare myself...

311
00:19:41,279 --> 00:19:44,243
That can't be.

312
00:19:44,631 --> 00:19:46,910
There's not a thing wrong with me,

313
00:19:47,126 --> 00:19:48,385
so why you?

314
00:19:48,410 --> 00:19:49,430
Excuse me.

315
00:19:49,932 --> 00:19:52,231
- Yes.
- I'm sorry.

316
00:19:53,432 --> 00:19:55,522
Letting you see me weak like this,

317
00:19:56,025 --> 00:19:57,998
when I swore you never would...

318
00:20:02,644 --> 00:20:04,475
Don't talk like that between us.

319
00:20:04,725 --> 00:20:08,251
Keep it up and I really will be upset.

320
00:20:12,532 --> 00:20:16,520
Will one be enough?

321
00:20:18,245 --> 00:20:20,579
I hear targeted therapy is expensive.

322
00:20:21,003 --> 00:20:22,799
Will that be enough to cover it?

323
00:20:27,734 --> 00:20:30,585
No, I'll manage on my own.

324
00:20:31,691 --> 00:20:34,775
Even if I died today,
I loved you with no regrets,

325
00:20:35,878 --> 00:20:37,118
and that's enough for me.

326
00:20:37,432 --> 00:20:39,338
No, I'm going to save you.

327
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,930
I'll save you whatever it takes,

328
00:20:42,169 --> 00:20:45,161
so don't ever worry about money.
Understood?

329
00:20:45,418 --> 00:20:46,425
Sweetheart.

330
00:20:54,906 --> 00:20:56,228
What do I do, Hui Na?

331
00:20:56,532 --> 00:20:58,128
My mom is seeing someone.

332
00:21:03,652 --> 00:21:06,385
That's not cheating.

333
00:21:06,387 --> 00:21:08,391
Your father passed away,

334
00:21:08,458 --> 00:21:10,569
so your mother can date, too.

335
00:21:11,005 --> 00:21:13,501
This isn't an ordinary romance.

336
00:21:13,752 --> 00:21:15,956
Of all people, she picked a swallow...

337
00:21:16,396 --> 00:21:19,340
A swallow? A bird? As in a bird?

338
00:21:29,659 --> 00:21:31,379
You can tell at a glance, can't you?

339
00:21:32,712 --> 00:21:34,795
A guy who clearly looks our age
or younger,

340
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:36,548
why else would he be seeing my mom?

341
00:21:39,999 --> 00:21:42,047
- It's obvious.
- Obvious, right?

342
00:21:42,049 --> 00:21:43,565
- A gigolo!
- A gigolo!

343
00:21:44,279 --> 00:21:46,292
- Exactly!
- What are you going to do?

344
00:21:46,849 --> 00:21:48,305
What do I do now?

345
00:21:48,586 --> 00:21:50,702
I think this bird has already taken
hundreds of thousands.

346
00:21:51,131 --> 00:21:52,575
Hundreds of thousands?

347
00:21:53,406 --> 00:21:56,912
Worse, there's no telling
how much more he'll bleed her for.

348
00:21:56,914 --> 00:21:58,892
Have you told your mother about this?

349
00:21:59,292 --> 00:22:00,305
No.

350
00:22:00,793 --> 00:22:02,626
If I let on, she'll cut me off.

351
00:22:02,626 --> 00:22:03,646
And I'd lose my inheritance.

352
00:22:04,059 --> 00:22:05,667
My brother knows all about it too,

353
00:22:05,735 --> 00:22:08,109
and he's keeping quiet
for the same reason.

354
00:22:08,134 --> 00:22:09,140
Hold on.

355
00:22:09,486 --> 00:22:10,490
Have you...

356
00:22:10,818 --> 00:22:12,773
looked into who this bird is?

357
00:22:13,641 --> 00:22:14,645
Just his number.

358
00:22:15,032 --> 00:22:16,410
I took it while she was showering.

359
00:22:16,797 --> 00:22:17,819
Give me the number.

360
00:22:19,172 --> 00:22:20,806
- What for?
- Quick.

361
00:22:21,156 --> 00:22:22,218
- What?
- Hurry.

362
00:22:22,432 --> 00:22:23,432
Hold on.

363
00:22:27,772 --> 00:22:28,786
He's finished.

364
00:22:30,046 --> 00:22:31,172
What are you doing?

365
00:22:36,472 --> 00:22:37,688
Pest control.

366
00:22:47,670 --> 00:22:48,733
Hello.

367
00:22:48,758 --> 00:22:50,972
Have you got nothing better to do
with your life?

368
00:22:54,304 --> 00:22:55,933
And what exactly am I doing?

369
00:22:56,279 --> 00:23:00,719
Seducing trusting women
and bleeding them dry, you gigolo.

370
00:23:01,619 --> 00:23:02,632
Who is this?

371
00:23:02,931 --> 00:23:04,412
Does it matter who I am?

372
00:23:04,671 --> 00:23:06,066
What are you going to do about it?

373
00:23:06,175 --> 00:23:07,666
Want to come seduce me too?

374
00:23:09,999 --> 00:23:13,213
You sound like a child,
and I don't do children.

375
00:23:13,239 --> 00:23:16,125
- Call me when you're older.
- Why, you...

376
00:23:17,912 --> 00:23:20,133
Does your mother know
this is how you live?

377
00:23:20,592 --> 00:23:25,369
Does she know you seduce
women her age and live like a parasite?

378
00:23:26,959 --> 00:23:28,198
I don't have a mother.

379
00:23:28,452 --> 00:23:29,690
Then does your father know?

380
00:23:30,371 --> 00:23:32,155
What, no father either?

381
00:23:32,484 --> 00:23:34,649
Are you an alien who fell out of the sky?

382
00:23:36,878 --> 00:23:38,944
I have everything on you.

383
00:23:38,946 --> 00:23:41,312
If you don't stop what you're doing,

384
00:23:41,346 --> 00:23:43,313
I'll go to your family. Your call.

385
00:23:43,578 --> 00:23:48,360
That their own son wrecks families
and lives well off the money,

386
00:23:48,534 --> 00:23:51,891
I'll go to them and expose
every last bit of it!

387
00:23:52,719 --> 00:23:54,683
Am I by any chance seeing your mother?

388
00:23:55,752 --> 00:23:56,972
Are you Min Ju?

389
00:23:56,973 --> 00:23:58,324
And is your mother Choi Hye Suk?

390
00:24:03,388 --> 00:24:04,528
Hello?

391
00:24:04,962 --> 00:24:05,969
Hello?

392
00:24:06,444 --> 00:24:07,452
Hey!

393
00:24:07,938 --> 00:24:09,965
You gigolo!

394
00:24:25,312 --> 00:24:27,072
Why did you hang up?

395
00:24:27,079 --> 00:24:28,832
Had enough of eating good food, have you?

396
00:24:28,939 --> 00:24:30,905
How about a proper stretch behind bars?

397
00:24:31,406 --> 00:24:33,419
Just name the date.

398
00:24:33,466 --> 00:24:36,984
Since you're going anyway,
midsummer would be nice and sweltering.

399
00:24:37,218 --> 00:24:38,499
What do you think?

400
00:24:39,345 --> 00:24:41,252
If you've had your fun, let's stop here.

401
00:24:41,625 --> 00:24:45,225
I was going to take my share and vanish,
but keep pushing and I might just...

402
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:47,802
become your stepfather.

403
00:24:48,290 --> 00:24:50,507
Is that what you want? Say the word.

404
00:24:50,636 --> 00:24:52,751
Why couldn't I grant
my own daughter one wish?

405
00:24:52,753 --> 00:24:53,992
Being your stepfather and all.

406
00:24:54,017 --> 00:24:56,198
What did you say?

407
00:24:56,572 --> 00:24:59,097
You'll get what's coming to you.

408
00:24:59,513 --> 00:25:01,245
I'm already getting it,

409
00:25:02,006 --> 00:25:03,765
so you needn't worry about me.

410
00:25:04,879 --> 00:25:06,646
Your stepfather is very busy, so goodbye.

411
00:25:14,099 --> 00:25:17,275
This bird is completely beyond reasoning.

412
00:25:17,543 --> 00:25:18,986
What? What did the bird say?

413
00:25:19,806 --> 00:25:22,992
The number you have dialed
is switched off...

414
00:25:23,047 --> 00:25:24,228
He turned it off?

415
00:25:24,309 --> 00:25:25,559
Unbelievable!

416
00:25:26,264 --> 00:25:28,145
How do I finish him off?

417
00:25:50,199 --> 00:25:51,238
(Yeong Gyu)

418
00:25:51,239 --> 00:25:53,047
Honey, your phone is ringing.

419
00:25:53,460 --> 00:25:56,152
Could you answer it? I'll be right there.

420
00:25:56,177 --> 00:25:57,184
All right.

421
00:26:01,385 --> 00:26:02,692
It's about to stop.

422
00:26:05,905 --> 00:26:07,146
Hello?

423
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:12,318
Isn't this Chairman Jang Hun Tae's phone?

424
00:26:13,201 --> 00:26:15,522
Yes, he can't come to the phone...

425
00:26:15,783 --> 00:26:18,159
- at the moment.
- Yes?

426
00:26:18,959 --> 00:26:20,939
- One moment, please.
- Who is it?

427
00:26:27,572 --> 00:26:28,937
Yes, this is Jang Hun Tae.

428
00:26:29,819 --> 00:26:31,179
This is Han Gyu Yeong.

429
00:26:31,550 --> 00:26:33,065
You've left work early.

430
00:26:33,906 --> 00:26:36,685
Yes, my schedule finished early.

431
00:26:38,539 --> 00:26:41,367
Could I see you for a moment,
if that's all right?

432
00:26:42,032 --> 00:26:43,039
Now?

433
00:26:43,831 --> 00:26:45,336
Yes, now.

434
00:26:47,780 --> 00:26:49,005
Is it urgent?

435
00:26:50,239 --> 00:26:51,605
I'll explain when I see you.

436
00:26:52,665 --> 00:26:53,874
All right, let's meet.

437
00:26:54,235 --> 00:26:55,452
Where should...

438
00:26:56,288 --> 00:26:57,466
Yes, I know it.

439
00:26:58,144 --> 00:27:01,389
Then I'll head over in about 30 minutes.

440
00:27:01,991 --> 00:27:02,998
All right.

441
00:27:06,379 --> 00:27:08,248
What could be so urgent...

442
00:27:08,516 --> 00:27:10,172
that she needs to see you after hours?

443
00:27:11,145 --> 00:27:13,879
I know. She said she'd explain in person.

444
00:27:14,845 --> 00:27:17,152
Will you be eating out?

445
00:27:17,452 --> 00:27:18,472
No.

446
00:27:18,946 --> 00:27:20,980
I've already smelled the fish stew,

447
00:27:21,393 --> 00:27:23,637
so I'll meet her quickly
and come home to eat with you.

448
00:27:24,072 --> 00:27:25,485
Shall I get your clothes?

449
00:27:26,706 --> 00:27:29,702
I can manage. Go on with your work.

450
00:27:50,312 --> 00:27:51,386
What's this?

451
00:27:52,546 --> 00:27:54,459
The money you lent me.

452
00:27:57,391 --> 00:28:01,070
Thanks to your help I graduated
and studied abroad without trouble.

453
00:28:01,492 --> 00:28:04,639
I was lucky enough to meet
a wonderful man there and get engaged.

454
00:28:05,032 --> 00:28:06,051
Is that so?

455
00:28:07,537 --> 00:28:08,645
Wonderful.

456
00:28:09,046 --> 00:28:10,827
I'll accept it gladly.

457
00:28:12,871 --> 00:28:15,521
And congratulations on the engagement.

458
00:28:18,013 --> 00:28:20,536
But shouldn't your mother...

459
00:28:20,561 --> 00:28:22,936
be told the news?

460
00:28:24,178 --> 00:28:25,192
No.

461
00:28:25,788 --> 00:28:28,845
I told his family my mother had passed.

462
00:28:31,969 --> 00:28:35,989
My family stopped counting her among
the living long ago.

463
00:28:36,825 --> 00:28:39,837
And it's better for your household too.

464
00:28:45,359 --> 00:28:46,372
Instead,

465
00:28:47,249 --> 00:28:48,575
in place of my mother,

466
00:28:49,636 --> 00:28:50,968
would you help me just once?

467
00:28:51,114 --> 00:28:54,552
No, actually, twice?

468
00:28:55,645 --> 00:28:56,678
Sorry?

469
00:29:00,258 --> 00:29:02,198
At the family meeting and the ceremony,

470
00:29:02,914 --> 00:29:05,565
you'd only have to pretend
to be my father twice...

471
00:29:07,538 --> 00:29:08,936
Has your father passed away?

472
00:29:10,046 --> 00:29:12,445
Last I knew, he was still alive.

473
00:29:13,786 --> 00:29:14,929
He is alive.

474
00:29:15,319 --> 00:29:17,743
- And?
- He's alive,

475
00:29:18,131 --> 00:29:22,132
but presenting him to others
is embarrass... I mean, difficult.

476
00:29:27,186 --> 00:29:28,766
Even so, that's...

477
00:29:29,012 --> 00:29:30,793
My future in-laws...

478
00:29:30,818 --> 00:29:33,782
are far, far above my family's level.

479
00:29:34,479 --> 00:29:36,811
I wanted so badly
to marry into that family,

480
00:29:37,018 --> 00:29:39,574
and not feel small, so I lied.

481
00:29:40,406 --> 00:29:41,839
That my mother had died,

482
00:29:42,754 --> 00:29:44,199
and my father was a businessman.

483
00:29:46,559 --> 00:29:48,952
I thought about hiring a stand-in,

484
00:29:49,130 --> 00:29:53,452
but you're not a stranger,
so asking you seemed better.

485
00:29:58,552 --> 00:29:59,891
You must think this is absurd.

486
00:30:03,065 --> 00:30:06,161
I know you're thinking,
"Has she lost her mind?"

487
00:30:07,403 --> 00:30:08,951
but if you met my father,

488
00:30:09,237 --> 00:30:11,352
you'd understand why I'm doing this.

489
00:30:13,945 --> 00:30:15,398
Please help me, sir.

490
00:30:29,820 --> 00:30:34,566
Sir! What do you take Han Seok Jung for?

491
00:30:34,722 --> 00:30:38,248
Do I look like a man who'd take your money
and run off somewhere?

492
00:30:39,410 --> 00:30:41,069
I'm hurt, sir.

493
00:30:41,904 --> 00:30:42,912
Sorry?

494
00:30:43,692 --> 00:30:45,652
You asked why I speak
with a Gyeongsang accent?

495
00:30:46,526 --> 00:30:49,052
Didn't I tell you before?

496
00:30:49,626 --> 00:30:52,353
You and I are from the same hometown.

497
00:30:52,408 --> 00:30:53,425
Yes.

498
00:30:53,926 --> 00:30:55,891
From your hometown of Tongyeong,

499
00:30:55,925 --> 00:30:58,358
head straight down and there's Bijindo...

500
00:30:58,599 --> 00:30:59,609
Sorry?

501
00:31:00,310 --> 00:31:01,319
Sorry?

502
00:31:02,372 --> 00:31:05,459
Not Tongyeong but Suncheon?

503
00:31:05,467 --> 00:31:08,645
What did I just say?

504
00:31:08,746 --> 00:31:10,712
Did I say Tongyeong just now?

505
00:31:10,966 --> 00:31:12,532
I could scream.

506
00:31:12,732 --> 00:31:15,918
I could bite my tongue and drop dead.
How ridiculous.

507
00:31:16,246 --> 00:31:17,972
Yes, sir,

508
00:31:18,299 --> 00:31:21,266
I'm Suncheon born and bred,

509
00:31:21,452 --> 00:31:23,821
and I nearly failed to recognize...

510
00:31:23,823 --> 00:31:25,998
a man from my own hometown.

511
00:31:27,089 --> 00:31:29,038
Listen, sir,

512
00:31:29,332 --> 00:31:31,752
let's not do this. How do I put it,

513
00:31:31,984 --> 00:31:35,202
with that warm Suncheon spirit
between lads,

514
00:31:35,483 --> 00:31:37,081
do me this one favor.

515
00:31:37,269 --> 00:31:38,279
Yes.

516
00:31:39,198 --> 00:31:43,577
I'd never run off
with your money, I swear.

517
00:31:43,704 --> 00:31:44,712
Yes.

518
00:31:44,737 --> 00:31:48,616
Sir, give me a little slack.

519
00:31:50,432 --> 00:31:51,445
Hello?

520
00:31:52,169 --> 00:31:53,522
Hello? Sir,

521
00:31:53,524 --> 00:31:54,905
Sir.

522
00:31:54,907 --> 00:31:56,755
Sir! Hello?

523
00:31:58,429 --> 00:31:59,765
He hung up.

524
00:32:06,198 --> 00:32:07,305
Gyu O.

525
00:32:10,719 --> 00:32:13,929
I said we'd meet at the pub,
so why did you bring me up here?

526
00:32:14,932 --> 00:32:16,759
What if our family sees us?

527
00:32:22,245 --> 00:32:23,589
This is the last time. I mean it.

528
00:32:25,959 --> 00:32:27,679
I know.

529
00:32:30,646 --> 00:32:32,768
You could've withdrawn
one big note instead.

530
00:32:32,902 --> 00:32:34,563
Why so many bills?

531
00:32:35,090 --> 00:32:36,496
They just take up space.

532
00:32:38,306 --> 00:32:40,246
Cleaning up your money messes,

533
00:32:40,248 --> 00:32:42,479
me doing it instead of Gyu Rim,
this is the last time.

534
00:32:43,747 --> 00:32:45,199
I said I know.

535
00:32:46,298 --> 00:32:48,902
From now on, whether you go to prison
or drop dead, it's not my problem.

536
00:32:48,927 --> 00:32:50,192
You clean up your own mess.

537
00:32:51,232 --> 00:32:53,259
Is my own son threatening me now?

538
00:32:54,539 --> 00:32:56,348
Especially if you bother Gyu Rim,

539
00:32:56,496 --> 00:32:58,045
I won't let it go.

540
00:32:59,606 --> 00:33:01,368
Won't let it go? What,

541
00:33:01,603 --> 00:33:02,692
are you going to hit me?

542
00:33:04,507 --> 00:33:05,765
How many did I count?

543
00:33:06,500 --> 00:33:07,625
I've forgotten.

544
00:33:08,333 --> 00:33:09,999
I'll start over.

545
00:33:10,387 --> 00:33:11,501
Give me the money.

546
00:33:11,502 --> 00:33:14,830
I hear you took Gyu Seo
and Gyu Min's allowance too?

547
00:33:15,078 --> 00:33:16,612
Took? Hardly.

548
00:33:17,119 --> 00:33:20,840
I just said my one wish was to stuff
myself with Korean beef,

549
00:33:21,047 --> 00:33:23,406
so Gyu Min gave me a bit
for imported beef instead.

550
00:33:23,465 --> 00:33:24,938
And Gyu Seo gave me nothing.

551
00:33:25,032 --> 00:33:27,146
- Just give me the money.
- Then promise me.

552
00:33:27,332 --> 00:33:29,285
That you won't bother
Gyu Rim, Gyu Min, or Gyu Seo.

553
00:33:29,632 --> 00:33:31,444
Promise you won't trouble them again.

554
00:33:32,045 --> 00:33:33,805
All right, I said all right.

555
00:33:33,950 --> 00:33:35,612
So hand over the money, you brat.

556
00:33:35,672 --> 00:33:37,652
Giving something and taking it back
is the lowest thing there is.

557
00:33:40,639 --> 00:33:42,092
Does Gyu O owe you money?

558
00:33:44,092 --> 00:33:45,935
I asked, does he owe you money?

559
00:33:46,186 --> 00:33:47,912
When will you grow up, Dad?

560
00:33:48,439 --> 00:33:50,776
Sooner than you. Why?

561
00:33:51,571 --> 00:33:54,707
You never buy me so much as a rice roll,

562
00:33:55,006 --> 00:33:57,152
and now you're raising your voice at me?

563
00:33:57,736 --> 00:33:58,945
Am I your fool?

564
00:33:59,176 --> 00:34:00,292
Hand it over.

565
00:34:00,966 --> 00:34:02,379
Don't take that money.

566
00:34:02,745 --> 00:34:04,875
Do you know what he did to earn it?

567
00:34:05,086 --> 00:34:06,412
Do you know how he earned it?

568
00:34:09,552 --> 00:34:11,405
Please don't take that money.

569
00:34:24,114 --> 00:34:25,346
What Gyu Seo said,

570
00:34:27,456 --> 00:34:28,639
what does he mean?

571
00:34:29,473 --> 00:34:30,596
Did you...

572
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:34,273
Did you rob someone for this money?

573
00:34:38,616 --> 00:34:39,709
Aren't you taking it?

574
00:34:39,734 --> 00:34:41,957
I asked what you did to get this money!

575
00:34:42,679 --> 00:34:45,349
- How did you earn it?
- What if I did?

576
00:34:46,192 --> 00:34:48,003
If it's dirty money, you don't need it?

577
00:34:48,439 --> 00:34:49,735
You won't spend it?

578
00:34:53,156 --> 00:34:54,824
Surely you didn't rob anyone.

579
00:34:56,045 --> 00:34:59,611
You are far too decent
and upright for that.

580
00:35:00,346 --> 00:35:04,230
Remember how you wanted to be a police
officer as a boy?

581
00:35:06,158 --> 00:35:08,060
As long as it isn't stolen, it's fine.

582
00:35:08,563 --> 00:35:12,092
Money is earned like a dog
and spent like a king.

583
00:35:16,066 --> 00:35:17,656
I'll count it later.

584
00:35:20,595 --> 00:35:21,665
I'm off.

585
00:35:39,052 --> 00:35:42,059
I don't know how much you think you know,
but stay out of it.

586
00:35:47,457 --> 00:35:49,074
How can I stay out of it?

587
00:35:49,686 --> 00:35:52,665
You're out there doing something insane.
How am I supposed to ignore it?

588
00:35:54,632 --> 00:35:57,894
Dad is hopeless, but you're the bigger
problem here.

589
00:35:58,496 --> 00:35:59,706
You know that?

590
00:36:15,106 --> 00:36:16,406
What is this?

591
00:36:16,846 --> 00:36:18,339
The money I've saved from part-time work.

592
00:36:22,452 --> 00:36:23,851
Why are you giving it to me?

593
00:36:24,826 --> 00:36:26,857
I might sign with a big agency soon.

594
00:36:27,699 --> 00:36:29,055
No, I will.

595
00:36:29,433 --> 00:36:31,791
So quit that insanity
before Gyu Rim finds out.

596
00:36:34,026 --> 00:36:36,209
If she learns how you're living,

597
00:36:37,874 --> 00:36:39,247
it will destroy her.

598
00:36:49,586 --> 00:36:52,019
Don't get cheeky.

599
00:36:53,318 --> 00:36:55,426
Forget part-time work and study.

600
00:36:55,833 --> 00:36:57,156
Aren't you a student?

601
00:36:58,066 --> 00:36:59,273
I'll give you a month.

602
00:37:00,406 --> 00:37:02,638
If you haven't stopped by then,

603
00:37:03,469 --> 00:37:05,007
I'll tell the whole family
what you've been doing.

604
00:37:08,613 --> 00:37:09,800
It's my life.

605
00:37:10,558 --> 00:37:13,823
I live it, I take responsibility,
and I earn my own money.

606
00:37:14,746 --> 00:37:17,121
So keep your mouth shut
and live your own life.

607
00:37:18,886 --> 00:37:20,014
How can I?

608
00:37:21,586 --> 00:37:23,473
If I were out there doing
the same garbage you are,

609
00:37:24,010 --> 00:37:26,106
could you just stand there and say,
"I'll mind my own life?"

610
00:37:26,806 --> 00:37:28,040
Could you really live like that?

611
00:37:28,339 --> 00:37:30,619
Yes, I could.

612
00:37:31,186 --> 00:37:32,739
I absolutely could.

613
00:37:33,332 --> 00:37:34,595
Don't lie.

614
00:37:36,146 --> 00:37:38,173
Just stop talking nonsense.

615
00:37:42,053 --> 00:37:44,162
I'm warning you one more time.

616
00:37:44,868 --> 00:37:46,379
Stay out of my life.

617
00:37:47,107 --> 00:37:49,894
If you run your mouth,
you'll answer to me.

618
00:37:50,435 --> 00:37:51,496
Understood?

619
00:38:02,026 --> 00:38:03,173
Planning to run again?

620
00:38:05,198 --> 00:38:06,667
If you're going to run, do it properly,

621
00:38:07,467 --> 00:38:08,869
so we never have to meet like this.

622
00:38:12,486 --> 00:38:15,173
What do I do?

623
00:38:15,198 --> 00:38:17,240
It's all burning!

624
00:38:21,885 --> 00:38:23,262
How did this happen?

625
00:38:23,432 --> 00:38:25,231
Did you fall asleep standing up?

626
00:38:26,688 --> 00:38:27,972
I'm sorry, Su Nam.

627
00:38:28,047 --> 00:38:31,184
We'd better open a window.

628
00:39:17,977 --> 00:39:19,564
What on earth is going on?

629
00:39:20,381 --> 00:39:22,974
This is the first time I've seen you cry.

630
00:39:24,312 --> 00:39:29,027
I'm not crying. These onions
are just too strong, Su Nam.

631
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:31,539
When have onions ever not been spicy?

632
00:39:31,699 --> 00:39:33,396
That's what makes them onions.

633
00:39:33,421 --> 00:39:36,002
If they weren't spicy,
would they even be onions?

634
00:39:36,166 --> 00:39:38,225
Even so, these are too strong.

635
00:39:38,686 --> 00:39:40,482
Let's change suppliers, Su Nam.

636
00:39:41,358 --> 00:39:45,067
Right. Change them at once.

637
00:39:45,160 --> 00:39:46,726
Let's change them right now.

638
00:39:47,071 --> 00:39:49,214
I'll ring Mr. Yang about it.

639
00:40:24,174 --> 00:40:25,446
Did you empty all of this?

640
00:40:28,006 --> 00:40:29,396
Why are you here instead of working?

641
00:40:30,466 --> 00:40:32,086
I'm gone, and now you too?

642
00:40:32,137 --> 00:40:35,429
How could I work after you left like that?

643
00:40:36,469 --> 00:40:37,939
Have you eaten?

644
00:40:39,046 --> 00:40:40,726
I was going to make myself a feast,

645
00:40:42,866 --> 00:40:44,291
but I burned it all.

646
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:50,339
So you poured all of this...

647
00:40:51,392 --> 00:40:53,316
on an empty stomach?

648
00:40:55,872 --> 00:40:57,130
Seems so.

649
00:40:58,412 --> 00:40:59,775
I'm not even drunk.

650
00:41:01,568 --> 00:41:02,773
Right.

651
00:41:03,105 --> 00:41:04,969
It would be stranger if you were fine.

652
00:41:08,806 --> 00:41:09,973
Want a drink?

653
00:41:10,176 --> 00:41:12,122
Forget the drink. For the life of me,

654
00:41:13,138 --> 00:41:14,713
I just can't make sense of it.

655
00:41:16,611 --> 00:41:17,899
What now?

656
00:41:19,110 --> 00:41:23,374
The Gyu Rim I know is not a woman
who'd see two men at once. Never.

657
00:41:23,514 --> 00:41:25,427
The Gyu Rim you know is the same, right?

658
00:41:26,672 --> 00:41:27,906
Let's stop talking about her.

659
00:41:27,931 --> 00:41:31,927
She must have met that monkey-faced man
after she left you.

660
00:41:32,099 --> 00:41:33,282
I said enough.

661
00:41:33,425 --> 00:41:35,543
But the boy is eight. Does that add up?

662
00:41:37,572 --> 00:41:39,832
You've been thinking
it doesn't add up either.

663
00:41:42,478 --> 00:41:43,506
And?

664
00:41:43,791 --> 00:41:44,906
Gyu Rim's son,

665
00:41:46,899 --> 00:41:48,389
I don't think he's that monkey's son.

666
00:41:50,069 --> 00:41:52,973
They look nothing alike.
If anything, he looks more like...

667
00:41:53,156 --> 00:41:54,941
The eyes, the nose...

668
00:41:56,604 --> 00:41:57,989
That's a stretch.

669
00:41:59,026 --> 00:42:01,774
Enough.
Stop writing fiction, Park Jeong Woo.

670
00:42:38,023 --> 00:42:39,240
Excuse me.

671
00:42:43,497 --> 00:42:45,863
Sorry. I thought you were someone I knew.

672
00:42:47,063 --> 00:42:48,229
Dad.

673
00:42:56,389 --> 00:42:57,847
You've got it bad. Really bad.

674
00:42:59,269 --> 00:43:00,347
Got what?

675
00:43:01,328 --> 00:43:04,419
You chased down a kid that size
yesterday too. Same line and all.

676
00:43:04,709 --> 00:43:06,758
"Sorry, I thought you
were someone I knew."

677
00:43:07,712 --> 00:43:10,916
Someone you knew? Who are you looking
for so desperately?

678
00:43:13,346 --> 00:43:16,658
Why? Is Han Gyu Rim's son
still on your mind?

679
00:43:23,737 --> 00:43:26,505
Your game account has been reactivated.

680
00:43:40,844 --> 00:43:43,113
What's got into him now?
He's making me nervous.

681
00:44:18,570 --> 00:44:21,223
Come shopping for clothes
with me at the department store.

682
00:44:22,306 --> 00:44:23,566
Why clothes all of a sudden?

683
00:44:23,951 --> 00:44:25,686
For meeting the in-laws.

684
00:44:25,762 --> 00:44:27,396
Who's meeting in-laws?

685
00:44:27,808 --> 00:44:29,648
- Gyu Yeong.
- What?

686
00:44:30,646 --> 00:44:32,866
I heard her on the phone
with a friend earlier.

687
00:44:33,227 --> 00:44:35,644
One o'clock today, Changdeokgung
in Gangnam.

688
00:44:36,734 --> 00:44:39,236
That's the famous marinated
beef ribs place, right?

689
00:44:49,726 --> 00:44:51,139
You're meeting the in-laws today?

690
00:44:52,825 --> 00:44:53,932
How did you know?

691
00:44:54,286 --> 00:44:57,659
You're meeting your in-laws
and I'm not supposed to know?

692
00:45:00,983 --> 00:45:02,173
This is so annoying.

693
00:45:02,612 --> 00:45:05,149
I won't be calling you,
so just pretend you don't know.

694
00:45:07,346 --> 00:45:10,856
How can I pretend? Are you an orphan?

695
00:45:10,881 --> 00:45:14,387
Yes, I said I was an orphan,
so stay out of it and let it go.

696
00:45:15,226 --> 00:45:17,206
How could you be an orphan?

697
00:45:17,434 --> 00:45:19,906
You have a father, a sister,
and younger siblings.

698
00:45:20,044 --> 00:45:21,389
Look how many of us there are.

699
00:45:21,646 --> 00:45:23,219
What you're doing is fraud.

700
00:45:25,964 --> 00:45:27,206
Han Gyu Yeong.

701
00:45:28,873 --> 00:45:30,848
So you're going there alone?

702
00:45:31,546 --> 00:45:35,846
Yes. I told them Mom died long ago
and Dad passed a few years back.

703
00:45:36,046 --> 00:45:38,026
And that my siblings are away on business.

704
00:45:39,526 --> 00:45:41,568
You told them I was dead?

705
00:45:42,286 --> 00:45:44,911
When I'm standing right here,
perfectly alive?

706
00:45:47,146 --> 00:45:48,482
This isn't right, Han Gyu Yeong.

707
00:45:49,357 --> 00:45:52,675
However far gone you are,
this isn't right.

708
00:45:53,326 --> 00:45:55,473
If I bring you and Dad along
and it ruins my marriage,

709
00:45:56,225 --> 00:45:57,480
will you take responsibility?

710
00:45:58,786 --> 00:46:01,383
Why would Dad and I ruin your marriage?

711
00:46:02,086 --> 00:46:05,800
Because this family is my shame,
my disgrace, my humiliation.

712
00:46:07,871 --> 00:46:09,884
What is she saying to us right now?

713
00:46:10,606 --> 00:46:13,442
Honestly, is there one decent person
among us?

714
00:46:13,726 --> 00:46:16,048
Is there anyone besides me
I could actually be proud of?

715
00:46:16,667 --> 00:46:18,953
Every one of you, uneducated,
second-rate, and ignorant.

716
00:46:22,666 --> 00:46:24,939
I'll buy the priciest clothes
at the department store,

717
00:46:25,686 --> 00:46:27,839
and say as little as possible
so the ignorance doesn't show.

718
00:46:28,606 --> 00:46:32,571
It won't stay hidden forever.
Lying like this isn't right.

719
00:46:33,106 --> 00:46:34,206
Right.

720
00:46:34,242 --> 00:46:38,622
When I'm properly dressed up,
people take me for a company president.

721
00:46:38,647 --> 00:46:40,490
I've already told them everything.

722
00:46:40,524 --> 00:46:42,873
I told them my father was dead.

723
00:46:44,098 --> 00:46:45,886
How many times will she kill me today?

724
00:46:53,454 --> 00:46:55,147
What do you mean?

725
00:46:55,509 --> 00:46:58,507
Where are you going that you can't
decide whether to go or not?

726
00:46:58,906 --> 00:47:02,926
I'll go if you say go,
and stay if you say stay.

727
00:47:04,604 --> 00:47:06,974
So where are you going?

728
00:47:08,093 --> 00:47:10,841
Someone asked me a favor, and it's...

729
00:47:13,046 --> 00:47:14,997
To stand in for her father
at a family meeting.

730
00:47:16,545 --> 00:47:18,312
Does she have no parents?

731
00:47:19,122 --> 00:47:21,406
I wouldn't know.

732
00:47:22,444 --> 00:47:24,106
Who is it that asked you?

733
00:47:25,606 --> 00:47:26,949
A distant relative.

734
00:47:27,766 --> 00:47:29,106
Someone I know too?

735
00:47:29,673 --> 00:47:31,339
You might.

736
00:47:33,766 --> 00:47:35,968
Someone I've met before?

737
00:47:37,366 --> 00:47:38,773
You've probably met her.

738
00:47:38,866 --> 00:47:40,066
Anyway, should I go or not?

739
00:47:42,613 --> 00:47:47,647
A relative, and you don't even know
if she has parents? That's strange.

740
00:47:48,073 --> 00:47:49,345
What's her name?

741
00:47:50,625 --> 00:47:51,722
Her name?

742
00:47:55,853 --> 00:47:57,343
- Goodness.
- Well...

743
00:47:57,579 --> 00:48:00,033
You don't know her name?
And she's a relative?

744
00:48:02,439 --> 00:48:06,036
Standing in at a family meeting
for someone whose name you don't know,

745
00:48:06,187 --> 00:48:07,400
does that make any sense?

746
00:48:08,446 --> 00:48:10,193
You're right. It doesn't.

747
00:48:11,386 --> 00:48:13,781
Then shall I not go?

748
00:48:16,958 --> 00:48:20,606
You should keep your head on straight.

749
00:48:20,654 --> 00:48:22,497
(Seonghan High School)

750
00:48:22,522 --> 00:48:23,606
Is this the right place?

751
00:48:24,166 --> 00:48:25,821
- It is.
- Hey.

752
00:48:27,539 --> 00:48:28,692
You're ashamed of me too, aren't you?

753
00:48:29,793 --> 00:48:34,451
You're so ashamed of me, but there's
no one else home, so you sent me?

754
00:48:35,266 --> 00:48:37,101
- What are you on about?
- Hey.

755
00:48:37,546 --> 00:48:40,366
Am I your disgrace,
your shame, your rock bottom too?

756
00:48:40,482 --> 00:48:41,846
Did Han Gyu Seo say that?

757
00:48:42,524 --> 00:48:43,836
Does he think so too?

758
00:48:44,217 --> 00:48:45,722
That boy, honestly.

759
00:48:45,812 --> 00:48:48,322
- Did Gyu O say it?
- Does he think so too?

760
00:48:49,038 --> 00:48:51,652
And I called that boy my son.

761
00:48:51,677 --> 00:48:53,580
So Han Gyu Yeong said it?

762
00:48:54,756 --> 00:48:55,906
Yes.

763
00:48:56,132 --> 00:48:59,606
That girl is meeting her in-laws today,
and she told them,

764
00:49:00,810 --> 00:49:01,960
I was dead.

765
00:49:02,713 --> 00:49:05,408
Gyu Yeong tore me to pieces.

766
00:49:06,536 --> 00:49:07,922
What are you talking about?

767
00:49:07,947 --> 00:49:09,892
That our whole family is an embarrassment.

768
00:49:10,752 --> 00:49:14,146
That no one should come, not you,
not anyone. That's what she said.

769
00:49:15,646 --> 00:49:17,210
I'm not going.

770
00:49:17,261 --> 00:49:19,113
I wouldn't lower myself to go either.

771
00:49:24,722 --> 00:49:25,863
Go on in.

772
00:49:26,351 --> 00:49:27,480
All right.

773
00:49:27,812 --> 00:49:29,236
You should at least say goodbye.

774
00:49:34,398 --> 00:49:35,547
That girl.

775
00:49:51,042 --> 00:49:53,059
Never mind. It's nothing.

776
00:49:53,513 --> 00:49:55,888
She thinks she's the finest thing alive.

777
00:49:56,086 --> 00:49:57,349
She'll sort herself out.

778
00:49:59,787 --> 00:50:01,206
That awful girl, really.

779
00:50:10,254 --> 00:50:12,256
Gyu Min, what is it at this hour?

780
00:50:13,227 --> 00:50:15,787
Dad just got in a taxi.
He's going to Han Gyu Yeong.

781
00:50:17,626 --> 00:50:18,739
What are you talking about?

782
00:50:18,928 --> 00:50:21,442
I told him to go and wreck it all.

783
00:50:22,306 --> 00:50:23,973
What do you mean?

784
00:50:24,149 --> 00:50:26,137
Han Gyu Yeong is meeting
her in-laws today, right?

785
00:50:27,106 --> 00:50:30,141
What? Dad went to where
she is meeting her in-laws?

786
00:50:42,406 --> 00:50:44,010
(Dad)

787
00:50:47,888 --> 00:50:49,303
Dad, please.

788
00:51:26,414 --> 00:51:28,306
- Gyu Yeong, you're here?
- Yes.

789
00:51:28,469 --> 00:51:30,039
You've arrived, ma'am.

790
00:51:31,358 --> 00:51:32,760
You must be tired
from coming all this way.

791
00:51:32,785 --> 00:51:33,985
You're here already, sweetheart?

792
00:51:34,666 --> 00:51:35,866
Is your father here?

793
00:51:36,512 --> 00:51:40,675
No. He said he'd be late
because of a meeting and sends apologies.

794
00:51:41,266 --> 00:51:43,066
He should be nearly here by now.

795
00:51:43,884 --> 00:51:45,513
We came early.

796
00:51:45,826 --> 00:51:47,739
Tell him not to worry and take his time.

797
00:51:48,346 --> 00:51:49,454
Yes, ma'am.

798
00:51:50,507 --> 00:51:52,360
Take your parents inside first.

799
00:51:52,511 --> 00:51:54,273
I'll come in with my father
when he arrives.

800
00:51:54,706 --> 00:51:56,146
All right. Shall we go in?

801
00:51:56,676 --> 00:51:57,787
Son.

802
00:51:57,846 --> 00:52:00,006
Your father and I will go in first,

803
00:52:00,398 --> 00:52:02,926
so bring her father in with you.

804
00:52:03,694 --> 00:52:05,644
It's fine. I'll bring him in myself.

805
00:52:06,107 --> 00:52:07,257
It's no trouble.

806
00:52:07,306 --> 00:52:08,866
- Do that.
- Yes.

807
00:52:15,884 --> 00:52:17,118
You go in too.

808
00:52:17,320 --> 00:52:18,356
No.

809
00:52:18,473 --> 00:52:21,307
So of course I should wait
and walk him in.

810
00:52:22,326 --> 00:52:23,856
Sweetheart.

811
00:52:28,706 --> 00:52:30,124
When will he get here?

812
00:52:31,757 --> 00:52:34,884
(Dad)

813
00:52:42,374 --> 00:52:43,452
Dad.

814
00:52:44,111 --> 00:52:46,061
I'm not too late, am I?

815
00:52:46,500 --> 00:52:48,075
Not at all. You're barely late.

816
00:52:48,773 --> 00:52:50,657
It's a pleasure to meet you, sir.
I'm Kang Seong Uk.

817
00:52:51,097 --> 00:52:52,472
Yes, good to meet you.

818
00:52:53,026 --> 00:52:54,466
Both his parents are already here.

819
00:52:54,586 --> 00:52:55,929
Let's go in, Dad.

820
00:52:58,846 --> 00:53:00,414
Yes, let's go in.

821
00:53:08,389 --> 00:53:11,026
- Where are you, Dad?
- I don't know either.

822
00:53:11,442 --> 00:53:12,639
Dad.

823
00:53:13,276 --> 00:53:14,639
Excuse me, where is this?

824
00:53:14,866 --> 00:53:16,786
- What neighborhood is this?
- Yaksu Dong.

825
00:53:18,073 --> 00:53:19,396
She says Yaksu Dong.

826
00:53:19,972 --> 00:53:21,273
Why are you there?

827
00:53:21,539 --> 00:53:22,926
Weren't you going to Gyu Yeong?

828
00:53:23,311 --> 00:53:24,973
I got out of the taxi on the way.

829
00:53:25,486 --> 00:53:26,773
I pictured myself turning up...

830
00:53:27,130 --> 00:53:30,461
and that girl losing her mind
and foaming at the mouth.

831
00:53:35,866 --> 00:53:38,713
My own daughter, and she frightens me.

832
00:53:39,826 --> 00:53:42,389
Excuse me, one bowl of rice, please.

833
00:53:42,639 --> 00:53:43,728
Yes.

834
00:53:44,191 --> 00:53:46,676
You did well. You were right to get out.

835
00:53:48,107 --> 00:53:49,273
You did well.

836
00:54:05,417 --> 00:54:06,751
Yes, a pleasure.

837
00:54:13,126 --> 00:54:16,223
This is pricey but a bit
lacking in flavor, isn't it?

838
00:54:18,469 --> 00:54:21,651
I said to prepare a Romanee-Conti
for a first meeting with in-laws.

839
00:54:24,766 --> 00:54:27,249
Honestly, I mostly drink
makgeolli or soju.

840
00:54:27,352 --> 00:54:28,723
I don't know much about wine.

841
00:54:29,866 --> 00:54:31,815
And with drinks this expensive,

842
00:54:32,377 --> 00:54:33,873
I don't think I could even
get drunk in peace.

843
00:54:34,781 --> 00:54:35,972
Quite right.

844
00:54:36,027 --> 00:54:38,090
Your father is so down-to-earth.

845
00:54:38,386 --> 00:54:40,906
And he looks like French nobility.

846
00:54:44,516 --> 00:54:47,004
How many guests are you thinking?

847
00:54:50,393 --> 00:54:53,888
Our family is on the smaller side, so...

848
00:54:55,214 --> 00:54:56,356
What do you think?

849
00:54:59,758 --> 00:55:01,675
I'd like a small wedding.

850
00:55:01,833 --> 00:55:04,109
Thirty at most?

851
00:55:05,076 --> 00:55:07,143
That few?

852
00:55:08,086 --> 00:55:11,113
We were thinking at least 150.

853
00:55:14,196 --> 00:55:16,836
Just invite as many as Gyu Yeong's side.

854
00:55:17,407 --> 00:55:19,492
Seong Uk, how could we?

855
00:55:19,606 --> 00:55:21,766
Then who do we invite
and who do we leave out?

856
00:55:23,884 --> 00:55:25,406
As you'll know, sir,

857
00:55:25,853 --> 00:55:29,732
in our world, politics and business
make everything a headache.

858
00:55:30,572 --> 00:55:33,829
The bigger they are, the more they sulk
over the smallest slight.

859
00:55:36,334 --> 00:55:38,728
What are your thoughts?

860
00:55:41,238 --> 00:55:44,421
Well, I'd like to do whatever they want.

861
00:55:45,406 --> 00:55:47,649
It's their marriage, after all.

862
00:55:49,419 --> 00:55:50,517
Yes.

863
00:55:51,586 --> 00:55:53,640
Let's get on well from now on.

864
00:55:54,566 --> 00:55:56,928
- Yes.
- Tell us if you ever need anything.

865
00:55:57,046 --> 00:55:59,960
- Just be kind to Gyu Yeong.
- Of course.

866
00:56:02,242 --> 00:56:04,535
I nearly forgot this.

867
00:56:07,246 --> 00:56:09,473
- What is it?
- The wedding gift list.

868
00:56:10,199 --> 00:56:12,038
I put together something simple.

869
00:56:12,406 --> 00:56:15,930
If your mother were here
she'd have handled it,

870
00:56:16,326 --> 00:56:20,158
but I didn't want you flustered
and lost on your own.

871
00:56:22,473 --> 00:56:24,506
Yes. Thank you, ma'am.

872
00:56:25,726 --> 00:56:27,989
Next time I'll invite you to our home.

873
00:56:28,052 --> 00:56:30,200
- Yes, thank you.
- Yes.

874
00:56:30,242 --> 00:56:33,046
- We'll be off then.
- Yes, see you soon.

875
00:56:33,817 --> 00:56:35,156
- I'm off.
- Take care.

876
00:56:36,239 --> 00:56:37,906
- I'll call you when I get home.
- All right.

877
00:56:38,381 --> 00:56:41,619
- Sir, we'll be going.
- Yes, see you again.

878
00:56:53,747 --> 00:56:55,007
(Wedding gift and Household Essentials)

879
00:57:03,466 --> 00:57:04,962
So did everything go well?

880
00:57:11,143 --> 00:57:12,772
Thank you so much for today.

881
00:57:13,906 --> 00:57:15,652
I was terrified you wouldn't come.

882
00:57:16,246 --> 00:57:19,366
But is this a marriage you have to have,
even if it takes all this?

883
00:57:22,378 --> 00:57:23,465
Yes.

884
00:57:23,913 --> 00:57:25,906
I've become an accomplice by accident,

885
00:57:27,105 --> 00:57:29,406
but this will wound your family,
and later,

886
00:57:29,762 --> 00:57:31,206
if his family finds out,

887
00:57:32,014 --> 00:57:33,292
it could become a serious problem.

888
00:57:33,317 --> 00:57:34,529
Can you take responsibility?

889
00:57:37,486 --> 00:57:39,026
I'll deal with that when it comes.

890
00:57:40,006 --> 00:57:42,173
Someone like you will never understand,

891
00:57:42,516 --> 00:57:44,209
but this marriage is one I need.

892
00:57:44,621 --> 00:57:46,461
One I have to have, even if it takes this.

893
00:57:53,812 --> 00:57:54,979
All right.

894
00:57:55,867 --> 00:57:57,506
I'll be going too.

895
00:57:59,866 --> 00:58:01,934
My mother was right to divorce.

896
00:58:05,177 --> 00:58:06,907
It's how she met someone as fine as you.

897
00:58:12,507 --> 00:58:13,661
I mean it.

898
00:58:37,636 --> 00:58:39,122
What is it? Something wrong?

899
00:58:39,732 --> 00:58:41,076
No. Nothing at all.

900
00:58:42,259 --> 00:58:43,391
By the way, where's Gyeol?

901
00:58:43,873 --> 00:58:45,210
I've been looking and can't find him.

902
00:58:45,686 --> 00:58:47,206
He's not in his room?

903
00:58:53,884 --> 00:58:56,278
- Yes, Mom.
- Where are you right now?

904
00:58:57,278 --> 00:59:00,027
Outside a burger place.
I came to meet someone.

905
00:59:00,386 --> 00:59:01,421
Who?

906
00:59:05,042 --> 00:59:06,305
The man from the game.

907
00:59:07,066 --> 00:59:08,642
Why would you meet him?

908
00:59:09,488 --> 00:59:12,073
He sent me game items.

909
00:59:12,398 --> 00:59:14,456
Only the most popular,
most expensive ones.

910
00:59:14,866 --> 00:59:16,786
Exactly the ones I wanted most.

911
00:59:17,146 --> 00:59:19,893
He seems like a better person
than I thought.

912
00:59:25,804 --> 00:59:28,065
Gyeol, why are you doing this too?

913
00:59:28,353 --> 00:59:30,604
You should have told me
about something like that.

914
00:59:31,006 --> 00:59:32,806
If you haven't met him yet, come home now.

915
00:59:33,189 --> 00:59:34,239
I already have.

916
00:59:40,846 --> 00:59:42,831
I'll be home soon. Don't worry.

917
00:59:45,105 --> 00:59:47,425
- Hello.
- Hello.

918
00:59:47,669 --> 00:59:49,698
I wanted to apologize. Properly.

919
00:59:50,814 --> 00:59:52,297
I'm the one who should apologize.

920
00:59:52,368 --> 00:59:55,362
For being rude to an adult.
I'm sorry, sir.

921
00:59:58,511 --> 01:00:00,250
Have you eaten?

922
01:00:00,419 --> 01:00:01,602
No.

923
01:00:01,993 --> 01:00:05,102
- Is a burger all right?
- Yes. It's my favorite food.

924
01:00:06,706 --> 01:00:09,886
I'm having the chicken mozzarella.

925
01:00:10,153 --> 01:00:12,311
That's my favorite too.

926
01:00:13,345 --> 01:00:16,815
- Toppings?
- No onions or pickles, add a fried egg.

927
01:00:18,046 --> 01:00:20,266
How are you exactly like me?
Shall we go in?

928
01:00:20,291 --> 01:00:21,331
Yes.

929
01:00:24,499 --> 01:00:26,937
The number you have dialed
is unavailable...

930
01:00:54,831 --> 01:00:57,438
(Mom)

931
01:00:59,568 --> 01:01:00,718
Answer it.

932
01:01:00,816 --> 01:01:01,957
It's all right.

933
01:01:04,040 --> 01:01:05,873
Who is it? Your mother?

934
01:01:13,747 --> 01:01:14,913
My mom.

935
01:01:15,873 --> 01:01:17,677
I said I'd be home soon.

936
01:01:20,330 --> 01:01:23,675
- Let's go.
- I haven't finished my burger.

937
01:01:23,877 --> 01:01:26,187
Eat at home. Hurry up.

938
01:01:27,307 --> 01:01:29,050
Hold on. I forgot my phone.

939
01:01:31,004 --> 01:01:32,174
Never mind.

940
01:01:37,412 --> 01:01:38,693
Gyu Rim.

941
01:01:41,459 --> 01:01:42,939
Could we talk for a moment?

942
01:01:45,219 --> 01:01:46,608
I have nothing to say.

943
01:01:48,046 --> 01:01:50,661
Don't be like that.
You should make up with him too.

944
01:01:50,913 --> 01:01:52,775
He seems like a really good person.

945
01:01:53,266 --> 01:01:55,931
Why? Because he sent you a few game items?

946
01:01:55,956 --> 01:01:57,427
And you fell for it that fast?

947
01:01:57,786 --> 01:02:01,271
You're already swayed by things like that.
I'm disappointed, Gyeol.

948
01:02:04,439 --> 01:02:05,533
Gyu Rim.

949
01:02:06,892 --> 01:02:10,092
My mom was really shaken
after the police station.

950
01:02:10,267 --> 01:02:11,778
She burned the kimchi pancakes.

951
01:02:12,205 --> 01:02:13,299
Go.

952
01:02:27,519 --> 01:02:28,973
Go on home first.

953
01:02:29,326 --> 01:02:31,520
I'll talk with him for a minute.

954
01:02:31,927 --> 01:02:34,171
To make up? Good thinking.

955
01:02:34,365 --> 01:02:36,238
Just make up properly, Mom.

956
01:02:37,145 --> 01:02:39,108
- Go.
- Yes. Good luck.

957
01:02:52,894 --> 01:02:56,850
Don't call my son out like this again.

958
01:02:58,033 --> 01:02:59,916
No notes, either,

959
01:03:00,288 --> 01:03:02,768
and no game items.

960
01:03:03,820 --> 01:03:05,005
I'm asking you.

961
01:03:05,866 --> 01:03:08,650
I'd rather we never meet like this again.

962
01:03:11,146 --> 01:03:12,680
There's something I want to know.

963
01:03:17,626 --> 01:03:18,973
Is he...

964
01:03:20,187 --> 01:03:21,373
my son?

965
01:03:29,573 --> 01:03:32,703
Is Gyeol my son?

966
01:04:04,976 --> 01:04:06,973
(Love on the Menu)

967
01:04:07,198 --> 01:04:09,173
I heard Gyeol is eight.

968
01:04:09,398 --> 01:04:10,725
And we broke up eight years ago.

969
01:04:10,750 --> 01:04:13,007
Were you seeing someone else
while you were with me?

970
01:04:13,084 --> 01:04:15,941
- Liar.
- Mom. Han Gyu Rim.

971
01:04:16,183 --> 01:04:18,465
- Yes, Gyeol.
- Why is my mom acting so strange?

972
01:04:18,520 --> 01:04:21,236
She's been very strange
since she met the man from the game.

973
01:04:21,387 --> 01:04:23,952
A negative plus a negative
makes a strong positive.

974
01:04:23,977 --> 01:04:25,861
It means you like it. A lot.

975
01:04:26,002 --> 01:04:27,929
- You know me, right?
- No, I don't.

976
01:04:27,954 --> 01:04:30,661
- Get a grip. I'm not your boyfriend.
- I know.

977
01:04:30,754 --> 01:04:32,923
Don't you think this is a bit much?

978
01:04:33,050 --> 01:04:34,545
Then will you buy the apartment,
Gyu Yeong?

979
01:04:34,570 --> 01:04:36,507
Han Gyu O. Do you have any money?

980
01:04:36,532 --> 01:04:40,175
Plenty of women brought you whatever
you needed when you struggled.

981
01:04:40,200 --> 01:04:41,694
It was Gyu Yeong's family meeting.

982
01:04:41,956 --> 01:04:44,098
Gyu Yeong. It's Mom.

983
01:04:44,372 --> 01:04:45,996
It's been a long time, Mom.

984
01:04:47,805 --> 01:04:49,805
Dramaday.me
